        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: St. John of the Cross Episcopal Church\n- Buildings: associated rectory\n- Architectural styles: Greek Revival architecture, Neoclassical architecture\n- Concepts: Hellenism\n\nFacts:\n- The associated rectory of St. John of the Cross Episcopal Church was built in 1830.\n- The associated rectory of St. John of the Cross Episcopal Church is a 1 1/2-story, rectangular, Greek Revival-style frame dwelling.\n- Greek Revival architecture is a product of Hellenism.\n- Greek Revival architecture may be regarded as the last phase in the development of Neoclassical architecture.",
